# Under a real Clock, the Session Host sleeps while the Foreground Run waits
# only for a deadline, answers the Foreground Run's `read` with a typed line,
# and pumps at each deadline a background Run waits for.
> on nap
|   wait 2 s
|   say "rested"
| end nap
> nap and wait
@ 2026-09-30T10:00:00Z
@ 2026-09-30T10:00:02Z
rested
> on echo
|   ask console to read and wait
|   say "got " & it
| end echo
> echo and wait
@ 2026-09-30T10:00:03Z
< hello
@ 2026-09-30T10:00:04Z
got hello
> on later
|   wait 5 s
|   say "later"
| end later
> send later to session
@ 2026-09-30T10:00:05Z
> 1 + 1
@ 2026-09-30T10:00:06Z
2
@ 2026-09-30T10:00:10Z
[session/r4] later
